WEBVTT

00:05.000 --> 00:10.500
I wrote this letter to sort out my feelings.

00:10.500 --> 00:15.000
I've realized that my life is a failure.
I'm nowhere near the person I want to be.

00:15.000 --> 00:19.500
I'm no scholar or athlete. I'm nothing to look at.
I'm short, and I'm not rich either.

00:19.500 --> 00:24.000
The older students and teachers I look up to,
the friends who've been kind to me… I fall short of them all.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.800
On TV and in books, they say everyone has at least one
good quality or talent. I looked and looked. I found nothing.

00:28.800 --> 00:33.000
My life is ordinary. I make no waves, for good or ill.
I'm just getting older. None of it means anything.

00:33.000 --> 00:38.000
Some things are useful even if they can't move or speak.
I can do both, and I'm still no use to anyone.

00:38.000 --> 00:44.000
Whatever I do, I'm average or worse. My report card is all B's.
Other people call me ordinary. Bland. Neither poison nor medicine.

00:44.000 --> 00:48.500
I went through life thinking I was something more.
My parents and relatives told me I was a good kid.

00:48.500 --> 00:53.000
My teachers called me diligent. The older students smiled
and said they could count on me.

00:53.000 --> 00:57.500
My friends said we'd always be close.
I took every word seriously. I never doubted any of it.

00:57.500 --> 01:01.500
But with so little to me,
could any of those words really have been true?

01:01.500 --> 01:08.000
I've only ever been good at keeping up appearances.
I've lived like a vine on a wall, taking whatever was there.
Could anyone really mean what they say to me?

01:08.000 --> 01:12.500
I know I don't mean it when I say those things myself.
And if even I can do that, of course everyone else can too.

01:12.500 --> 01:17.000
What makes me any different from a plant that just grows,
without a thought, even when it gets too little water or sun?

01:17.000 --> 01:21.000
Would a person walking by ever stop
and say anything to a plant like that?

01:21.000 --> 01:25.000
I have nothing. All I can do right now is daydream.
If only I were smarter.

01:25.000 --> 01:29.000
If only I were taller, better-looking, better at sports.
If only I had more money.

01:29.000 --> 01:32.000
Then my life would have been so much better.

01:32.000 --> 01:35.000
If I could be born again, I'd want to live a wonderful life.

01:35.000 --> 01:39.000
A life I could be proud to tell people about.
A life where people would speak to me and mean it.

01:39.000 --> 01:42.000
That's honestly how I feel right now.
And that's my next goal.

01:42.000 --> 01:46.000
The next time I read this letter,
will I be living a new life?

01:46.000 --> 01:50.000
I can't wait to see what my new life will be like.

01:50.000 --> 02:01.000
The Wonderful Self-Harm Guide
